192
00:12:35,852 --> 00:12:40,817
[SPEAKER_00]: He's just declaring it, because he's in the presence of a Samana Brahman, that...

193
00:12:41,639 --> 00:12:46,502
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he's just going along with it for whatever benefit he believes he's going to get from it.

194
00:12:46,522 --> 00:12:46,642
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

195
00:12:46,782 --> 00:12:47,642
[SPEAKER_01]: Some special mantra.

196
00:12:47,662 --> 00:12:48,803
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's no different at all.

197
00:12:48,823 --> 00:12:49,784
[SPEAKER_01]: Some special practice.

198
00:12:50,164 --> 00:12:51,164
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's...

199
00:12:51,645 --> 00:12:59,329
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, at that time, when he should be persuaded to undertake truthfulness, he's persuaded to undertake falsehood.

200
00:12:59,429 --> 00:13:00,529
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

201
00:13:00,770 --> 00:13:06,172
[SPEAKER_01]: At the end of the night, he resumes the consumption of his belongings.

202
00:13:06,192 --> 00:13:10,815
[SPEAKER_01]: He takes back his clothing and things and he's given up and nothing's his.

203
00:13:11,433 --> 00:13:14,976
[SPEAKER_01]: Even though they aren't given back to him, and he gave them up.

204
00:13:15,657 --> 00:13:16,317
[SPEAKER_01]: Right, right, right.

205
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:17,979
[SPEAKER_01]: This counts as stealing, it says, yeah.

206
00:13:18,139 --> 00:13:18,459
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

207
00:13:19,039 --> 00:13:23,823
[SPEAKER_01]: I tell you, such is the apostle of the giants, when this apostle of the giants is undertaken.

208
00:13:24,664 --> 00:13:25,045
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

209
00:13:25,085 --> 00:13:35,513
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he gave the example of the giants, because obviously it was probably prominent at the time, but you could see the principle of that is basically taking on the practice superficially.

210
00:13:36,614 --> 00:13:39,777
[SPEAKER_00]: And I think that's sort of what he describes the medals pretty much

211
00:13:40,314 --> 00:13:43,655
[SPEAKER_00]: Most of the temples today, where people go and take the precepts, because they offer the food.

212
00:13:43,715 --> 00:13:52,239
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they go through the motion of chanting the precepts, declaring the precepts, knowing, even beforehand, that the moment they leave the monastery, precepts won't apply to them.

213
00:13:52,819 --> 00:13:54,740
[SPEAKER_00]: They'll carry on drinking or whatever else.

214
00:13:55,780 --> 00:13:57,501
[SPEAKER_00]: But, it's done by both.

215
00:13:57,521 --> 00:14:02,463
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the monks are encouraging, exactly like giant scum good men, take the precepts, it's good for you, you make merit.

216
00:14:02,923 --> 00:14:07,725
[SPEAKER_00]: And they do so, both, while knowing it's just gonna be for the duration of the chant, and maybe till the end of the day,

217
00:14:09,511 --> 00:14:11,432
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, they go back to their own life.

218
00:14:11,512 --> 00:14:13,334
[SPEAKER_00]: Normally, nothing has changed.

219
00:14:14,434 --> 00:14:15,575
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's not really an opposite.

220
00:14:15,655 --> 00:14:25,082
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's a type of opposite, as you can see, like opposed on the surface, which is worse, because it's even more dishonest.

221
00:14:25,972 --> 00:14:36,237
[SPEAKER_00]: Because many people do genuinely believe, certainly traditional Buddhists, that by simply by taking the precepts, without the intention of keeping them, they are accruing merit somehow, somewhere.

222
00:14:36,698 --> 00:14:38,138
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, look, I am doing this.

223
00:14:38,238 --> 00:14:39,399
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I'm cleaning.

224
00:14:39,419 --> 00:14:40,940
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, it's a form of cleansing.

225
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:47,683
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, take your clothes, put these clothes, wash your hair, you know, bow to the four directions, whatever giant we're doing or other brahmins.

226
00:14:48,024 --> 00:14:48,784
[SPEAKER_00]: That's exactly it.

227
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:54,547
[SPEAKER_00]: Just going through the motions that obviously are kind of held together with the belief of

228
00:14:55,037 --> 00:14:57,598
[SPEAKER_00]: I went to church on a Sunday, said my prayers, cleared the week.

229
00:14:57,618 --> 00:14:59,019
[SPEAKER_00]: And what is the uposta of the noble ones?

230
00:15:23,879 --> 00:15:27,140
[SPEAKER_01]: It is the cleansing of the defiled mind through the proper technique.

231
00:15:28,301 --> 00:15:31,862
[SPEAKER_01]: And how is the defiled mind cleansed?

232
00:15:31,882 --> 00:15:32,943
[SPEAKER_01]: Through the proper technique.

233
00:15:35,544 --> 00:15:43,867
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is the case where a disciple of the Noble Ones, a noble disciple, recollects the Buddha.

234
00:15:44,568 --> 00:15:52,491
[SPEAKER_01]: Indeed, the Blessed One is worthy, rightly, self-awakened, consummate in knowledge and conduct, well-gone, an expert with regard to the world,

235
00:15:53,581 --> 00:16:01,203
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yes, faith in the teaching, in the teacher, the teaching.

236
00:16:01,623 --> 00:16:01,843
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

237
00:16:02,244 --> 00:16:06,565
[SPEAKER_01]: As he is recollecting like this, his mind is calmed.

238
00:16:06,925 --> 00:16:08,165
[SPEAKER_01]: Joy arises.

239
00:16:08,185 --> 00:16:14,027
[SPEAKER_01]: The defilements of his mind are abandoned, just as when the head is cleansed through proper technique.

240
00:16:15,070 --> 00:16:15,310
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

241
00:16:15,370 --> 00:16:17,292
[SPEAKER_01]: And it gives like through soap and so on.

242
00:16:17,512 --> 00:16:18,012
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

243
00:16:18,353 --> 00:16:20,534
[SPEAKER_00]: What I said, exactly what people believed.

244
00:16:20,634 --> 00:16:25,218
[SPEAKER_00]: By washing your your hands with the soap, with this water, in that direction, you're cleansing your mind.

245
00:16:25,959 --> 00:16:38,048
[SPEAKER_00]: But Buddha says, yes, through a technique of recollecting the Buddha, the dhamma, the saṅgha, on the basis of your right view, recollecting the quality of enlightenment, the path, the knowledge, you are cleansing your mind.

246
00:16:38,348 --> 00:16:42,772
[SPEAKER_00]: By bringing up and thinking about those contexts, those themes,

247
00:16:44,686 --> 00:17:04,615
[SPEAKER_00]: of enlightenment, awakening, freedom from suffering, on the basis of your right views, on the basis of seeing what your mind actually is, then, yes, that results in the actual purification, like what people believe of washing it, you know, the method and the motions of how you wash it and how you prostrate, like that.

248
00:17:04,795 --> 00:17:05,776
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how people believe it.

249
00:17:05,856 --> 00:17:07,396
[SPEAKER_00]: But this is what actually cleans your mind.

250
00:17:07,616 --> 00:17:09,097
[SPEAKER_01]: You're bowing down like this.

251
00:17:09,197 --> 00:17:09,497
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

252
00:17:09,637 --> 00:17:10,337
[SPEAKER_01]: Cleans the mind.

253
00:17:10,438 --> 00:17:11,498
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly, exactly.

254
00:17:12,325 --> 00:17:16,306
[SPEAKER_01]: The recollection of the Buddha on the basis of your right view... That cleans your mind.

255
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:17,826
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

256
00:17:18,206 --> 00:17:22,207
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the right themes, the right contemplations clean your mind.

257
00:17:23,348 --> 00:17:30,169
[SPEAKER_00]: As we said so many times, as the Buddha said in many suttas, what you often think and ponder about, that becomes the direction of your mind.

258
00:17:30,409 --> 00:17:32,690
[SPEAKER_00]: It's an inclination, it slopes, it goes that way.

259
00:17:33,510 --> 00:17:40,592
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you often think and ponder about liberation, suffering, the peril of sensuality, the mind will turn away from those things that are contradictory to that.

260
00:17:41,582 --> 00:17:46,564
[SPEAKER_00]: But that needs to be, like, yeah, observed regularly, sustained.

261
00:17:46,924 --> 00:17:47,584
[SPEAKER_01]: Thought about.

262
00:17:47,624 --> 00:17:48,484
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, exactly.

263
00:17:48,504 --> 00:17:49,045
[SPEAKER_00]: Thought about.

264
00:17:49,085 --> 00:17:49,645
[SPEAKER_00]: Pondered on.

265
00:17:50,585 --> 00:17:52,826
[SPEAKER_00]: Rekindle your zeal towards that.

266
00:17:54,226 --> 00:18:01,429
[SPEAKER_00]: Inspiration towards thinking those themes that kind of initially go against your experience and certainly against the experience of a central household life.

267
00:18:02,649 --> 00:18:10,572
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you think about them long enough, they will... the values behind those themes, those contexts, will take place, will take root,

268
00:18:10,969 --> 00:18:11,689
[SPEAKER_00]: We'll start to grow.

269
00:18:14,671 --> 00:18:18,693
[SPEAKER_01]: Because... you don't really hear about that often.

270
00:18:18,773 --> 00:18:20,674
[SPEAKER_01]: I just think about the Buddha and his qualities.

271
00:18:21,075 --> 00:18:29,679
[SPEAKER_00]: It's kind of... Well, because, yeah, people... Well, first of all, as with many other suttas, people ignore the fact that you need to be a Sotāpanna first for that to apply to you.

272
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:33,601
[SPEAKER_00]: Having ignored that fact, then it becomes easy to... Oh, yeah, of course.

273
00:18:34,282 --> 00:18:35,182
[SPEAKER_00]: We already do that.

274
00:18:36,163 --> 00:18:39,985
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's taken for granted that everybody already does that.

275
00:18:40,677 --> 00:18:41,377
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's great.

276
00:18:41,517 --> 00:18:44,518
[SPEAKER_00]: But you realize, well, actually, follow further in the same sutta.

277
00:18:45,158 --> 00:18:49,279
[SPEAKER_00]: These are the results that should follow, if you do that rightly, on the basis of the right view.

278
00:18:49,319 --> 00:18:51,160
[SPEAKER_00]: So, do you have the results to follow?

279
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:56,181
[SPEAKER_00]: Is your mind inspired because you think you are saved by the Lord Buddha?

280
00:18:57,702 --> 00:19:03,323
[SPEAKER_00]: Or is your mind inspired because it's incapable of lust and aversion towards very unfavorable circumstances?

281
00:19:04,438 --> 00:19:09,519
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the confidence towards, I cannot be defiled internally, confidence comes on account of it.

282
00:19:09,999 --> 00:19:15,680
[SPEAKER_00]: Is that your zeal, your inspiration, or because the Lord Buddha is always looking over you and everything will work out?

283
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:16,960
[SPEAKER_00]: It's different.

284
00:19:17,241 --> 00:19:17,521
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

285
00:19:18,141 --> 00:19:18,681
[SPEAKER_00]: Which one is it?

286
00:19:19,961 --> 00:19:26,962
[SPEAKER_00]: Or maybe not specifically such a kind of personified idea of the Lord Buddha, but do you hold the belief that everything will work out?

287
00:19:28,263 --> 00:19:29,123
[SPEAKER_00]: Everything will be fine for you.

288
00:19:29,383 --> 00:19:30,323
[SPEAKER_00]: Where is that belief rooted?

289
00:19:31,270 --> 00:19:38,076
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it a factual recognition of your right view, sotāpati, so you know you are beyond the states of peril and so on?

290
00:19:39,698 --> 00:19:48,526
[SPEAKER_00]: Factual recognition of the purified states of mind that you know for fact, like you see them, pure and impure, you avoid impure, you cultivate the pure?

291
00:19:49,087 --> 00:19:50,228
[SPEAKER_00]: Or is it just wishful thinking?

292
00:19:50,648 --> 00:19:51,409
[SPEAKER_00]: Everything will work out.

293
00:19:51,529 --> 00:19:52,250
[SPEAKER_00]: On the basis of what?

294
00:19:52,930 --> 00:19:53,571
[SPEAKER_00]: On the basis of what?

295
00:19:53,611 --> 00:19:54,712
[SPEAKER_00]: You have such observance.

296
00:19:58,066 --> 00:20:04,851
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you can start imagining the Buddha, these images in your mind.

297
00:20:04,871 --> 00:20:07,993
[SPEAKER_00]: Maybe you won't do that, but do you dig down, believe that everything worked out?

298
00:20:08,994 --> 00:20:11,375
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, but fine, you have that belief, no problem.

299
00:20:11,715 --> 00:20:12,716
[SPEAKER_00]: What do you do in account with?

300
00:20:14,117 --> 00:20:23,243
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you, like, put that belief first, and then all the effort, the renunciation, reflection, giving up that you have to do, that you know you have to do if you want to practice dhamma?

301
00:20:23,663 --> 00:20:24,244
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you kind of

302
00:20:24,902 --> 00:20:30,805
[SPEAKER_00]: Try your best and, you know, but deep down believe that everything will work out, although you are not really putting the effort first.

303
00:20:31,845 --> 00:20:34,526
[SPEAKER_00]: Or are you really putting the effort first and disregarding the belief?

304
00:20:34,606 --> 00:20:35,987
[SPEAKER_00]: Whether it's there or not doesn't matter.

305
00:20:36,027 --> 00:20:37,528
[SPEAKER_00]: What matters is whether you make the effort.

306
00:20:38,548 --> 00:20:42,090
[SPEAKER_00]: And that always comes back to that simile of the the chicken with its eggs.

307
00:20:43,530 --> 00:20:49,893
[SPEAKER_00]: If a chicken, even if she wishes, every minute of her life, may these chicks, my chicks, pierce safely from these shells,

308
00:20:51,018 --> 00:20:54,981
[SPEAKER_00]: But she doesn't sit on the eggs long enough, well enough, often enough, they won't.

309
00:20:55,682 --> 00:20:59,184
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, you have the other chick, whether even she doesn't wish for the chicken.

310
00:20:59,585 --> 00:21:03,207
[SPEAKER_00]: Whether she doesn't wish for the chicks to pierce out, they will, because she is doing the work.

311
00:21:04,168 --> 00:21:05,089
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's always like...

312
00:21:05,189 --> 00:21:06,530
[SPEAKER_00]: So, are you putting the work first?

313
00:21:07,010 --> 00:21:10,733
[SPEAKER_00]: Or you believe that everything will work out and you're doing your best?

314
00:21:11,253 --> 00:21:12,194
[SPEAKER_00]: Or are you putting that first?

315
00:21:13,095 --> 00:21:14,716
[SPEAKER_00]: Because otherwise, it's a bit too much pressure.

316
00:21:18,271 --> 00:21:20,972
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah, you do... are you doing the Jain prasada?

317
00:21:21,492 --> 00:21:22,472
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

318
00:21:22,632 --> 00:21:32,795
[SPEAKER_00]: Again, these are like the obvious kind of clean-cut examples, but you could... if you discern the principle, you could see how it would apply to many of the contemporary things that are... that are done and placed.

319
00:21:32,875 --> 00:21:33,455
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

320
00:21:35,815 --> 00:21:39,116
[SPEAKER_01]: Purification through mantra, purification through incense, whatever.

321
00:21:39,136 --> 00:21:42,037
[SPEAKER_00]: Through... through techniques, through methods, purification through

322
00:21:42,493 --> 00:21:48,194
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, I won't have to think, sustain, ponder on danger, and develop the context, and reflect, and get the right view first.

323
00:21:48,795 --> 00:21:50,835
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll just do this exercise, pretty much.

324
00:21:50,855 --> 00:21:57,537
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll just watch my nostrils like this, walk like this, attend to this, feel like this, and then I'll be purified.

325
00:21:57,557 --> 00:22:08,800
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's like, the only way for purification to occur is if you already can and have seen the signs of your mind, the phenomenon, the cittanimitta, for what it is.

326
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:10,640
[SPEAKER_00]: If you basically have the right view.

327
00:22:11,343 --> 00:22:17,248
[SPEAKER_00]: Without the right view, the domain where purification happens, is just invisible to you.

328
00:22:17,828 --> 00:22:35,321
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why often, without the right view, any such practice does kind of imply, to some degree, you know, when everybody starts the practice, you're new to it, you get your ideas, and the idea of enlightenment, insight, sotāpatti, it always has almost like this, requires this magical leap.

329
00:22:36,022 --> 00:22:40,225
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, I'm doing all this stuff, I'm committed, I'm doing these practices, and then,

330
00:22:40,851 --> 00:22:46,555
[SPEAKER_00]: The right view will happen to me, or arahantship will happen to me.

331
00:22:46,575 --> 00:22:51,118
[SPEAKER_00]: Means you don't really see where purification is and where it happens, because that's where it happens.

332
00:22:51,439 --> 00:22:54,701
[SPEAKER_00]: When you purify it, that's what the right view is, when the mind is purified enough.

333
00:22:55,602 --> 00:23:01,266
[SPEAKER_00]: But in order to purify it enough, you can't just wish for it to happen on account of these observances you're doing.

334
00:23:03,527 --> 00:23:06,870
[SPEAKER_00]: Only if you see it where it needs to be purified, what it needs to be purified.

335
00:23:08,191 --> 00:23:09,932
[SPEAKER_00]: If you start seeing what the mind is,

336
00:23:10,500 --> 00:23:13,983
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why, as the sutta says, cittanimitta is the prerequisite for the right view.

337
00:23:16,064 --> 00:23:18,566
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, you know exactly what the practice is.

338
00:23:18,887 --> 00:23:22,650
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, there is no more magical leaps involved, or doing this for this to happen.

339
00:23:23,270 --> 00:23:24,251
[SPEAKER_00]: You know exactly.

340
00:23:24,271 --> 00:23:26,072
[SPEAKER_00]: Wholesome intention, unwholesome intention.

341
00:23:26,573 --> 00:23:27,373
[SPEAKER_00]: Cultivating one's...

342
00:23:27,413 --> 00:23:28,254
[SPEAKER_01]: Dirt and cleanliness.

343
00:23:28,314 --> 00:23:28,494
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

344
00:23:28,574 --> 00:23:29,335
[SPEAKER_00]: Dirt and cleanliness.

345
00:23:29,635 --> 00:23:36,080
[SPEAKER_00]: And you see exactly what needs to be cleaned, and how, and to what extent.

346
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:38,682
[SPEAKER_01]: That's when you can start the work.

347
00:23:38,722 --> 00:23:39,263
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

348
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:42,321
[SPEAKER_00]: That's at least when you know what the work is.

349
00:23:43,182 --> 00:23:44,083
[SPEAKER_00]: Now you see it clearly.

350
00:23:44,103 --> 00:23:47,025
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's all, you know, you reason, you measure the task.

351
00:23:47,665 --> 00:23:48,846
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, this is what needs to be done.

352
00:23:48,866 --> 00:23:50,207
[SPEAKER_00]: You see what it needs to be done.

353
00:23:50,327 --> 00:23:52,509
[SPEAKER_00]: And then it's easy to do it, because now you see it.

354
00:23:53,589 --> 00:24:01,495
[SPEAKER_00]: But when it's all like sort of, you know, at arm's length, with certain kind of magical leaps in connection, just hoping for it to happen, then

355
00:24:03,946 --> 00:24:06,007
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, it's on the level of wishful thinking.

356
00:24:06,067 --> 00:24:09,848
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, whatever happens, you don't even know if it's good or bad, important or unimportant.

357
00:24:10,228 --> 00:24:12,448
[SPEAKER_00]: You're already bent on it being the right thing.

358
00:24:13,389 --> 00:24:19,010
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's when people start interpreting any mundane stuff as spiritual stuff, because of the context of their spiritual practice.

359
00:24:21,531 --> 00:24:30,693
[SPEAKER_00]: But if they didn't have the context of the spiritual practice that they developed, their inspiration, you would just see it as just the mundane stuff, which is some new experience.

360
00:24:31,623 --> 00:24:34,525
[SPEAKER_00]: Novelty this, novelty that, there's nothing to it.

361
00:24:34,585 --> 00:24:40,188
[SPEAKER_00]: But no, there's much more to it, because of my already pre-decided belief that there will be a lot more to it, because I'm practicing.

362
00:24:40,808 --> 00:24:44,790
[SPEAKER_00]: And that does go hand in hand with that view that everything will work out.

363
00:24:46,131 --> 00:24:57,217
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whatever I'm doing, on account of my inspiration to practice dhamma, doesn't matter whether I see it, whether it's directly related, how it's related, whether it's bringing our wholesome to increase,

364
00:24:57,713 --> 00:25:00,294
[SPEAKER_00]: Wholesome to decrease or wholesome to increase, unwholesome.

365
00:25:00,694 --> 00:25:03,074
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't matter if I see that clearly, if I fully understood it.

366
00:25:03,394 --> 00:25:04,494
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't matter if I see the saṅgha.

367
00:25:04,654 --> 00:25:05,875
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't matter if I have the right view.

368
00:25:06,895 --> 00:25:10,236
[SPEAKER_00]: I do have the pure, wholesome intention to practice the dhamma.

369
00:25:10,776 --> 00:25:16,897
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, whatever I do on account of that, it's towards the goal of nibbāna and the dhamma, and I'll be fine.

370
00:25:17,937 --> 00:25:19,657
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's a very dangerous view to have.

371
00:25:20,358 --> 00:25:22,458
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, as we said in previous talks,

372
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:29,044
[SPEAKER_00]: In the suttas, one of the definitions of the right view is knowing important as important and unimportant as unimportant.

373
00:25:29,644 --> 00:25:35,867
[SPEAKER_00]: Without knowing that, people end up doing unimportant as important and overlooking the important.

374
00:25:37,488 --> 00:25:44,673
[SPEAKER_00]: And often people do overlook, like... See, the Buddha describes exactly how to calm your mind, how to experience joy, how to purify your mind, if you have the right view.

375
00:25:45,593 --> 00:25:46,574
[SPEAKER_00]: Think these themes.

376
00:25:47,454 --> 00:25:48,255
[SPEAKER_00]: Sustain them.

377
00:25:48,335 --> 00:25:49,015
[SPEAKER_00]: Observe them.

378
00:25:49,135 --> 00:25:50,756
[SPEAKER_00]: Make an observance out of them.

379
00:25:51,312 --> 00:25:53,053
[SPEAKER_00]: For many people, that's exactly as you said.

380
00:25:53,873 --> 00:25:54,954
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yeah, that's just thinking.

381
00:25:56,354 --> 00:25:57,995
[SPEAKER_00]: That's not as important.

382
00:25:58,055 --> 00:25:58,235
[SPEAKER_00]: See?

383
00:25:58,876 --> 00:26:02,917
[SPEAKER_00]: The attitude for somebody who would say, well, that's just merely thinking about the Buddha.

384
00:26:03,798 --> 00:26:04,778
[SPEAKER_00]: That's not as important.

385
00:26:05,158 --> 00:26:06,559
[SPEAKER_00]: There must be something more important.

386
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:07,900
[SPEAKER_00]: And there you go.

387
00:26:07,980 --> 00:26:09,480
[SPEAKER_00]: You overlooked what's actually important.

388
00:26:11,201 --> 00:26:12,682
[SPEAKER_00]: And went further and you lost it.

389
00:26:14,783 --> 00:26:15,783
[SPEAKER_00]: But that is what's important.

390
00:26:18,344 --> 00:26:19,445
[SPEAKER_00]: Do it long enough, you'll see it.

391
00:26:24,198 --> 00:26:25,079
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, but that's just thinking.

392
00:26:25,859 --> 00:26:26,920
[SPEAKER_00]: That's just contemplation.

393
00:26:28,020 --> 00:26:28,681
[SPEAKER_00]: Anybody can do that.

394
00:26:28,701 --> 00:26:30,302
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, but how many people actually do it like that?

395
00:26:31,042 --> 00:26:32,823
[SPEAKER_00]: How many people do it on the basis of the right view?

396
00:26:35,705 --> 00:26:41,388
[SPEAKER_00]: But exactly, whoever reads that, many people would read that, and you almost don't even read it anymore.

397
00:26:41,528 --> 00:26:43,229
[SPEAKER_00]: You just, oh yeah, Buddha, Dhamma, Saṅgha, of course.

398
00:26:43,489 --> 00:26:44,830
[SPEAKER_00]: I approve of that.

399
00:26:45,651 --> 00:26:46,051
[SPEAKER_00]: No, no, no.

400
00:26:46,431 --> 00:26:47,251
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you observe it?

401
00:26:47,291 --> 00:26:49,393
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you make a theme to ponder on these qualities?

402
00:26:49,413 --> 00:26:50,133
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you dig them up?

403
00:26:50,834 --> 00:26:51,514
[SPEAKER_00]: Revisit them?

404
00:26:52,114 --> 00:26:53,195
[SPEAKER_00]: Establish your mind

405
00:26:54,094 --> 00:26:57,695
[SPEAKER_00]: Basically, develop inspiration towards those... Not like...

406
00:26:58,175 --> 00:27:01,616
[SPEAKER_00]: When I say inspiration, I don't mean uplifting of faith where everything will work out.

407
00:27:01,916 --> 00:27:02,696
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm inspired.

408
00:27:03,196 --> 00:27:03,316
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

409
00:27:03,356 --> 00:27:06,877
[SPEAKER_00]: Inspiration to think more about you what you already been thinking.

410
00:27:06,897 --> 00:27:11,158
[SPEAKER_00]: To really get even more clarity in regard to... to what needs to be understood.

411
00:27:13,678 --> 00:27:16,419
[SPEAKER_00]: But, again, if you think that it's... Oh, that's just that.

412
00:27:16,459 --> 00:27:16,979
[SPEAKER_00]: That's obvious.

413
00:27:16,999 --> 00:27:17,879
[SPEAKER_00]: That's self-evident.

414
00:27:18,659 --> 00:27:20,099
[SPEAKER_00]: You overlooked the important.

415
00:27:20,219 --> 00:27:21,660
[SPEAKER_00]: You see this not so important.

416
00:27:21,860 --> 00:27:21,980
[SPEAKER_00]: I...

417
00:27:22,100 --> 00:27:22,740
[SPEAKER_00]: It's unimportant.

418
00:27:27,302 --> 00:27:30,024
[SPEAKER_01]: Let's go through the second.

419
00:27:30,485 --> 00:27:36,089
[SPEAKER_01]: There is the case where a disciple, a noble disciple, recollects the dhamma also, you said.

420
00:27:38,171 --> 00:27:41,794
[SPEAKER_01]: And... or recollects the saṅgha.

421
00:27:42,775 --> 00:27:44,316
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, you see, like recollects the dhamma.

422
00:27:45,597 --> 00:27:46,798
[SPEAKER_00]: Does not mean you recollect...

423
00:27:46,818 --> 00:27:47,899
[SPEAKER_00]: I recollect the dhamma.

424
00:27:48,019 --> 00:27:48,940
[SPEAKER_00]: The dhamma is the great.

425
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:49,160
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

426
00:27:49,240 --> 00:27:54,765
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollects any aspect, practical aspect of the Buddhist enlightenment, the teacher, what he teaches.

427
00:27:55,545 --> 00:28:06,970
[SPEAKER_00]: So, recollect the dhamma through recollecting any relevant context, theme, on account of which you kind of have the right view already, that can now further it even more.

428
00:28:08,391 --> 00:28:09,872
[SPEAKER_00]: But, yeah, dhamma is the great.

429
00:28:09,932 --> 00:28:11,072
[SPEAKER_00]: Dhamma is the greatest teaching.

430
00:28:11,092 --> 00:28:14,814
[SPEAKER_00]: No, don't recollect it in a personal, kind of glorifying sense.

431
00:28:15,534 --> 00:28:17,335
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollect it in the same sense.

432
00:28:17,715 --> 00:28:21,237
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollecting the quality of the Buddha, the teacher, it's well-expounded, i.e.

433
00:28:21,537 --> 00:28:23,938
[SPEAKER_00]: it's worth committing to, personally,

434
00:28:24,658 --> 00:28:27,805
[SPEAKER_00]: It's worth for me to commit to the teaching of this teacher.

435
00:28:28,567 --> 00:28:33,739
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yes, there is some faith involved, but only so that you can do it and start seeing it for yourself.

436
00:28:36,466 --> 00:28:40,648
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not about worshipping the saṅgha?

437
00:28:40,708 --> 00:28:47,471
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it's not about worshipping the Buddha either, nor the saṅgha, nor the dhamma, the teaching, the great tipiṭaka.

438
00:28:47,611 --> 00:28:49,972
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's bow to it.

439
00:28:50,012 --> 00:28:55,514
[SPEAKER_00]: Involving yourself personally with it, so that you can start doing it, so that you can become free from suffering.

440
00:28:55,914 --> 00:29:01,316
[SPEAKER_00]: And again, all of these recollections don't require you to meet the Buddha, nor the saṅgha for that matter.

441
00:29:02,217 --> 00:29:03,237
[SPEAKER_00]: You just recognize.

442
00:29:03,257 --> 00:29:05,818
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, the teaching, freedom from suffering,

443
00:29:06,600 --> 00:29:15,563
[SPEAKER_00]: Having obviously understood enough, initially, where the problem is, where the mind is, develop the right view, now recollect the same.

444
00:29:15,603 --> 00:29:24,927
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollect the quality of the Buddha, the teacher, how what he said you should do and practice and develop, it's worth, because you can see it for yourself already, the benefits and the results of it.

445
00:29:25,367 --> 00:29:33,570
[SPEAKER_00]: So, just keep reminding yourself of that, sustain that as a context, then your mind will... well, will become unable to... to be defiled.

446
00:29:36,549 --> 00:29:42,192
[SPEAKER_01]: And something I left out was, when recollecting the dhamma, the samādhi is like cleaning your body.

447
00:29:42,613 --> 00:29:44,614
[SPEAKER_01]: So, recollecting the Buddha is cleaning your head.

448
00:29:44,994 --> 00:29:45,695
[SPEAKER_01]: Right, right, right.

449
00:29:45,715 --> 00:29:46,655
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a good practice.

450
00:29:47,235 --> 00:29:50,737
[SPEAKER_01]: And recollecting the samādhi would be cleaning your clothes, putting on new clothes, fresh clothes.

451
00:29:50,777 --> 00:29:51,598
[SPEAKER_00]: It's all about cleansing.

452
00:29:51,618 --> 00:29:52,038
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

453
00:29:54,340 --> 00:29:54,840
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh...

454
00:29:57,498 --> 00:30:02,421
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is a case where the noble disciple recollects his own virtues, right?

455
00:30:02,681 --> 00:30:11,845
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, my virtues are unbroken, unspotted, unsplattered, untarnished, liberating, praised by the wise, conducive to samādhi, to composure.

456
00:30:12,946 --> 00:30:19,709
[SPEAKER_01]: As he's recollecting his virtue, his mind is calm, joy arises, the defilements of his mind are abandoned.

457
00:30:19,810 --> 00:30:22,451
[SPEAKER_01]: Just as when a mirror is cleansed through proper technique.

458
00:30:22,791 --> 00:30:25,032
[SPEAKER_00]: So, now the example is cleaning a mirror.

459
00:30:25,112 --> 00:30:25,492
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's that.

460
00:30:25,532 --> 00:30:26,513
[SPEAKER_00]: Again, that's the technique.

461
00:30:28,388 --> 00:30:34,292
[SPEAKER_00]: Recollection, context on the basis of factual sense restraint and not giving in to unwholesome behavior.

462
00:30:35,913 --> 00:30:40,056
[SPEAKER_00]: Keeping the virtue unbroken, recollecting it, gladness, joy, samādhi.

463
00:30:40,436 --> 00:30:41,377
[SPEAKER_00]: That is what samādhi is.

464
00:30:42,137 --> 00:30:43,878
[SPEAKER_00]: Established context of the right kind.

465
00:30:45,479 --> 00:30:46,320
[SPEAKER_00]: And the technique?

466
00:30:47,641 --> 00:30:51,824
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like the technique of cleaning the mirror, the mechanical technique of cleaning the mirror.

467
00:30:52,744 --> 00:30:56,927
[SPEAKER_00]: Except, you realize up there is nothing mechanical can be done about it.

468
00:30:58,655 --> 00:30:59,496
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the thing.

469
00:30:59,516 --> 00:31:03,360
[SPEAKER_00]: If you start mechanically recollecting the virtue, the dhamma, the saṅgha... You won't last long.

470
00:31:03,661 --> 00:31:03,981
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

471
00:31:04,362 --> 00:31:04,822
[SPEAKER_00]: You won't last.

472
00:31:04,862 --> 00:31:07,405
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why all people need something more palpable.

473
00:31:07,665 --> 00:31:12,451
[SPEAKER_00]: No, but tell me what to do, you know, with my body, with my attention, with my sensations.

474
00:31:12,611 --> 00:31:14,012
[SPEAKER_00]: Tell me something more palpable.

475
00:31:14,032 --> 00:31:17,977
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it must recollect my own virtues.

476
00:31:20,101 --> 00:31:21,642
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yeah, that would also be the thing.

477
00:31:21,802 --> 00:31:23,043
[SPEAKER_01]: So... Do I keep five precepts?

478
00:31:23,263 --> 00:31:23,543
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

479
00:31:23,763 --> 00:31:25,564
[SPEAKER_00]: Eight precepts, five precepts, eight precepts.

480
00:31:25,584 --> 00:31:26,605
[SPEAKER_00]: And what is the result of that?

481
00:31:26,625 --> 00:31:27,805
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the result of that?

482
00:31:27,886 --> 00:31:29,526
[SPEAKER_00]: Uplifting... Where are my values?

483
00:31:29,747 --> 00:31:29,907
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

484
00:31:30,607 --> 00:31:32,448
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you start realizing where your values are.

485
00:31:33,128 --> 00:31:34,629
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it on the value of the shepherd?

486
00:31:36,750 --> 00:31:39,332
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, oh, I want this, I do it, I want that, now I do this?

487
00:31:40,152 --> 00:31:41,313
[SPEAKER_00]: Or is it on the value... No, hold on.

488
00:31:42,353 --> 00:31:49,097
[SPEAKER_00]: This observance of the precepts, it needs to be undertaken, like, infinitely, for the rest of my life.

489
00:31:51,384 --> 00:31:58,226
[SPEAKER_00]: And I said that before, you know, it's better to take the five precepts for the rest of your life, than eight precepts on the weekend.

490
00:31:58,607 --> 00:31:58,927
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

491
00:31:59,987 --> 00:32:08,130
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you will feel the weight of it, the context of it, and that's already a better basis for... then you can take eight within that, and so on, but you will never go below five.

492
00:32:08,990 --> 00:32:16,493
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you're just taking occasionally, picking and choosing, your spiritual practice becomes like the shepherd's desires.

493
00:32:16,593 --> 00:32:17,093
[SPEAKER_00]: I want this,

494
00:32:17,479 --> 00:32:18,359
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, now I have too much of it.

495
00:32:18,419 --> 00:32:19,840
[SPEAKER_00]: Now I want a spiritual practice.

496
00:32:19,960 --> 00:32:25,161
[SPEAKER_00]: Up until I forget, then I want back to this, then to this, and it's just flopping from one to the other.

497
00:32:25,481 --> 00:32:25,702
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

498
00:32:25,982 --> 00:32:26,662
[SPEAKER_01]: Unbeneficial.

499
00:32:26,682 --> 00:32:27,142
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

500
00:32:31,023 --> 00:32:34,304
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is a case where a noble disciple recollects the devas.

501
00:32:35,544 --> 00:32:43,987
[SPEAKER_01]: So, actually, there are these devas in these heavens, these great kings and so on, who have the power over others' creations.

502
00:32:44,687 --> 00:32:47,248
[SPEAKER_01]: He thinks about all these other heavens, heavenly realms.

503
00:32:51,321 --> 00:32:51,501
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

504
00:32:51,541 --> 00:32:53,342
[SPEAKER_01]: Conviction, I think it means faith.

505
00:33:16,592 --> 00:33:16,972
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

506
00:33:17,012 --> 00:33:23,934
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever factors, whatever generosity they had, whatever discernment they had, all those things are present within me.

507
00:33:24,334 --> 00:33:26,535
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why those beings went to heaven.

508
00:33:26,835 --> 00:33:27,295
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

509
00:33:27,335 --> 00:33:38,158
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, you can... you can feel confident that the worst-case scenario, if you don't take your right view further, you'll at least be in the heavens.

510
00:33:40,019 --> 00:33:45,160
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the worst-case scenario, which is not a bad scenario, from the human point of view.

511
00:33:48,581 --> 00:33:49,983
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm still going to a good place.

512
00:33:50,643 --> 00:33:52,746
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm still headed in the right.

513
00:33:52,766 --> 00:33:57,751
[SPEAKER_00]: And even if you say, well, but I don't, you know, I don't see the devas and the kings and so on.

514
00:33:59,213 --> 00:34:03,137
[SPEAKER_00]: You have faith in the Buddha, on account of which you practiced and developed the right view.

515
00:34:03,597 --> 00:34:05,239
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you see for yourself freedom from suffering.

516
00:34:05,319 --> 00:34:08,903
[SPEAKER_00]: You see for yourself the benefit of faith, virtue, discernment.

517
00:34:09,643 --> 00:34:15,666
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, the same source, the Buddha, who taught you these things that are kind of impossible to see.

518
00:34:15,706 --> 00:34:17,947
[SPEAKER_00]: You realize the depth of the dhamma when you get the right view.

519
00:34:18,007 --> 00:34:21,209
[SPEAKER_00]: You realize how it's... how it cannot be obtained by accident.

520
00:34:21,909 --> 00:34:26,732
[SPEAKER_00]: How it is truly a miracle that sort of, you know, the self-awakened one discovered and taught to others.

521
00:34:27,812 --> 00:34:34,135
[SPEAKER_00]: And now, he says these other things about rewards in heavens that I don't necessarily see, but I have absolutely no basis to doubt it.

522
00:34:34,316 --> 00:34:39,058
[SPEAKER_00]: Because what, you know, what pertains to the core of the holy life has been understood,

523
00:34:40,725 --> 00:34:45,606
[SPEAKER_00]: And he came from the same source that also says, and see, if you don't get anywhere, at least you'll be in heaven.

524
00:34:46,627 --> 00:34:53,268
[SPEAKER_00]: Because Sariputta, the second after the Buddha, in terms of this sermon, couldn't see the heaven or understand the devas or anything.

525
00:34:54,088 --> 00:34:58,689
[SPEAKER_00]: He had faith in them, they were real, because obviously the Buddha said so, but he couldn't see any of it.

526
00:34:59,369 --> 00:35:06,411
[SPEAKER_00]: To the point of that sutta where he heard somebody ask him about, he heard that, oh, there's these devas that live

527
00:35:07,508 --> 00:35:11,493
[SPEAKER_00]: Many of them live on the single-placed... No, space on a needle.

528
00:35:12,494 --> 00:35:18,581
[SPEAKER_00]: And they don't feel crowded and confined with each other, because their minds are so lofty and developed.

529
00:35:20,022 --> 00:35:27,511
[SPEAKER_00]: And Sariputra thought what to make of it, and he says, oh, it's because they practiced... they developed their minds over there.

530
00:35:29,145 --> 00:35:29,845
[SPEAKER_00]: That was his answer.

531
00:35:30,246 --> 00:35:32,626
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, on the basis of reasoning here and now.

532
00:35:32,906 --> 00:35:33,907
[SPEAKER_00]: He didn't see the devas.

533
00:35:34,047 --> 00:35:35,947
[SPEAKER_00]: He couldn't see how and why.

534
00:35:35,987 --> 00:35:38,308
[SPEAKER_00]: He couldn't talk to them, as some other monks could.

535
00:35:39,329 --> 00:35:42,430
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, the devas heard that and told the Buddha to tell him that he was wrong.

536
00:35:42,810 --> 00:35:46,791
[SPEAKER_00]: And actually, it was their minds developed during the human life.

537
00:35:46,831 --> 00:35:48,011
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where the practice is.

538
00:35:48,292 --> 00:35:49,632
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, they're enjoying benefits.

539
00:35:50,592 --> 00:35:51,953
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, the Buddha told that to Sariputta.

540
00:35:51,973 --> 00:35:52,613
[SPEAKER_00]: He was like, oh, yeah.

541
00:35:53,293 --> 00:35:54,474
[SPEAKER_00]: But he couldn't see it for himself.

542
00:35:56,014 --> 00:35:56,994
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's a kind of...

543
00:35:58,833 --> 00:36:03,415
[SPEAKER_00]: It can be the extension of the faith, but it's also, again, just to calm your mind down.

544
00:36:06,056 --> 00:36:21,622
[SPEAKER_00]: If there's pressure, disturbances, but you do have the right view, but you might be overwhelmed, nevertheless, illness, something's happening, whatever else, hardships, bearing too much of the elements is just adding up, reflect on these things and you get samādhi as a result of it.

545
00:36:22,042 --> 00:36:24,263
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, as I said, it did come from the same source.

546
00:36:24,883 --> 00:36:28,625
[SPEAKER_00]: The source that taught you the right view, and not to suffer amid suffering,

547
00:36:29,548 --> 00:36:53,463
[SPEAKER_00]: We also talked about these other rewards, that why would he have a reason to lie, if he already showed you something that no other teaching shows you, that doesn't require anything from you, doesn't require worship, doesn't require some weird kind of sacrificial, just requires good virtue, which is good regardless of the religion, not killing, not stealing, not cheating, not lying.

548
00:36:54,084 --> 00:36:55,845
[SPEAKER_00]: It's good regardless of what your views are.

549
00:36:56,949 --> 00:37:01,052
[SPEAKER_00]: Sensory strength, not engaging in sensuality, that's verifiable here and now.

550
00:37:01,292 --> 00:37:05,475
[SPEAKER_00]: It's burden, it's unpleasant, it's peril, it results in more, more weight.

551
00:37:06,056 --> 00:37:07,356
[SPEAKER_00]: All things you can see for yourself.

552
00:37:08,357 --> 00:37:09,978
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it's freed me from all those things.

553
00:37:09,998 --> 00:37:12,600
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's always like one of the first... come and see for yourself.

554
00:37:12,660 --> 00:37:14,822
[SPEAKER_00]: When people ask you what you're teaching, come and see for yourself.

555
00:37:15,162 --> 00:37:21,907
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't... By all means, I urge you to not take it merely on faith and inspiration and how radiant I look or something.

556
00:37:23,028 --> 00:37:24,889
[SPEAKER_01]: No, the Buddha said to come and see for yourself.

557
00:37:27,158 --> 00:37:47,252
[SPEAKER_01]: The last bit is, furthermore, the disciple of the noble ones, noble disciple, reflects thus, as long as they live, the arahants abandon the taking of life, abstain from the taking of life, dwell with their weapons laid down, so on, compassionate for the welfare of all living beings.

558
00:37:48,713 --> 00:37:53,156
[SPEAKER_01]: Today, I too, for this day and night, abandoning the taking of life,

559
